@using NFHotel.Application.Dto.Bookings
@using NFHotel.Application.Dto.Guests
@using NFHotel.Application.Dto.Rooms
@using NFHotel.Application.Dto.Holidays
@using NFHotel.Application.Errors
@using NFHotel.Application.Ports
@using NFHotel.Application.UseCases
@using NFHotel.Application.UseCases.Bookings
@using NFHotel.Application.UseCases.Guests
@using NFHotel.Application.UseCases.Rooms
@using NFHotel.Domain.Repositories

@*
    The receipt for one booking. Used both as step 4 in the flow and on /my-booking, the own booking of a guest whom
    /booking has signed in with the reference and the email of the booking (MIL-018, ADR-0049).

    BR-C-06 — WHY THERE IS NO NAME HERE
    The card takes BookingReceiptDto, which has only the reference, the period, the number of nights, the room type and
    the status (BR-C-05, ADR-0049 decision 7). There is no guest in it, so the card cannot show a name, an email or a
    phone number, not even by mistake. Before MIL-079 the card took the whole booking, while the number alone opened the
    page: FLZ-000123 was one digit from the next guest's booking. MIL-079 made the number open the receipt only together
    with the email of the booking, MIL-018 made the two sign the guest in, and MIL-085 replaced the number with a random
    reference that cannot be worked out from another booking (ADR-0049 decision 1).

    There is no price either. The price model does not exist in Phase 1 (BR-C-05, BR-31), and
    "Payment on arrival" is the honest answer rather than an empty field that looks like a fault.
*@

@if (Receipt is not null)
{
    <article class="card card-pad stack pub-receipt">
        <div class="stack-sm">
            <span class="eyebrow">Booking reference</span>
            <p class="pub-receipt-reference">@ReferenceText</p>
            <p class="muted">Keep this reference. With the email you booked with, it opens this booking again.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="divider"></div>

        <dl>
            <dt>Check-in</dt>
            <dd class="numeric">@PublicDateText.Long(Receipt.StartDate)</dd>

            <dt>Check-out</dt>
            <dd class="numeric">@PublicDateText.Long(Receipt.EndDate)</dd>

            <dt>Length of stay</dt>
            <dd class="numeric">@PublicDateText.Nights(Receipt.Nights)</dd>

            <dt>Room type</dt>
            <dd>@RoomText</dd>

            <dt>Status</dt>
            <dd><StatusBadge BookingStatus="Receipt.Status" /></dd>

            <dt>Price</dt>
            <dd>@BookingFlowViewModel.PaymentText</dd>
        </dl>
    </article>
}
